    {
      "filename": "California-06376 - Ferry Building (20450110740).jpg",
      "title": "File:California-06376 - Ferry Building (20450110740).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d2/California-06376_-_Ferry_Building_%2820450110740%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:California-06376_-_Ferry_Building_(20450110740).jpg",
      "width": 1080,
      "height": 1920,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Dennis G. Jarvis",
      "description": "The clock tower was designed after the 12th-century Giralda bell tower in Seville, Spain, and the entire length of the building on both frontages is based on an arched arcade.\nDesigned in 1892, the ferry building was completed in 1898. At its opening, it was the largest project undertaken in the city up to that time. \nWith decreased use after bridges were constructed across the bay to carry railroad traffic, in the 1950s, the building was adapted for office use and its public spaces were broken up in an unsympathetic manner.\n\nIn 2002, a restoration and renovation were undertaken to redevelop the entire complex. The 201 m (660 ft) long Great Nave was restored, together with its height and materials. A marketplace was created for the ground floor, the former baggage handling area. The second and third floors were adapted for office and Port Commission use.",
      "dateCreated": "2015-08-07 17:08",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "san-francisco-ferry-building-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "9q8z",
      "smallPath": "_m/9/q/8/z/san-francisco-ferry-building-wp/california-06376-ferry-buildin-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "California-06368 - Ferry Building (20450104830).jpg",
      "title": "File:California-06368 - Ferry Building (20450104830).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/53/California-06368_-_Ferry_Building_%2820450104830%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:California-06368_-_Ferry_Building_(20450104830).jpg",
      "width": 1080,
      "height": 1920,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Dennis G. Jarvis",
      "description": "The San Francisco Ferry Building is a terminal for ferries that travel across the San Francisco Bay, a food hall, and also has offices, located on The Embarcadero.\nOn top of the building is a 74.7 m (245 ft) tall clock tower, with four clock dials, each 22 feet in diameter. During daylight, on every full and half-hour, the clock bell chimes portions of the Westminster Quarters. \nThe clock tower was designed after the 12th-century Giralda bell tower in Seville, Spain, and the entire length of the building on both frontages is based on an arched arcade.\nDesigned in 1892, the ferry building was completed in 1898. At its opening, it was the largest project undertaken in the city up to that time. \nWith decreased use after bridges were constructed across the bay to carry railroad traffic, in the 1950s, the building was adapted for office use and its public spaces were broken up in an unsympathetic manner.\n\nIn 2002, a restoration and renovation were undertaken to redevelop the entire complex. The 201 m (660 ft) long Great Nave was restored, together with its height and materials. A marketplace was created for the ground floor, the former baggage handling area. The second and third floors were adapted for office and Port Commission use.",
      "dateCreated": "2015-08-07 17:03",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "san-francisco-ferry-building-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "9q8z",
      "smallPath": "_m/9/q/8/z/san-francisco-ferry-building-wp/california-06368-ferry-buildin-small.webp"
    },
